    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0756" n="746" xml:id="pg746"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-23T12:00:00+08:00">March 23,
                            1949—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 23—3:54 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>629. New Premier<anchor n="33" xml:id="d698-f1"/> came to see me Sunday evening
                    to discuss chaotic financial situation and its mortal threat to his Cabinet in
                    the making. He requested US support for Chinese currency, suggesting a kind of
                    stabilizing loan of “2 or 300 million dollars”. He said that unless support in
                    some degree were forthcoming from abroad promptly, new government if formed
                    could not survive nor could it be expected to hold its own in any peace talks
                    with Communists. I made no comment other than that I would transmit his request
                    to my Government. Our comments follow separately.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d698-f2"
                    />
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Canton 182, Shanghai 288.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
